: "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn8le13ob08re2img05.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn8le13ob08re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn8le13ob08re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn8le13ob08re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa:</span> Hey, what's that?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> I'm not sure.  It's a letter of some kind.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa:</span> Does the address look familiar? It might be from a long lost relative.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Oh my goodness!\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa:</span> Calm down and let me see. Someone has written you a poem? Well ... that's different!\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Wow ... This is from Christian from work.  I think it's a Valentine's Day poem.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa:</span> He wrote you a poem?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> This is the sweetest thing I have ever read. It even rhymes. It's long too - 3 stanzas.  This must have taken him ages. You could read it aloud for me.", "id": 1}, {"time": "39000", "image": "engenn8le13ob08re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa:</span> <br />My Valentine, you're all I see;<br />\nIn you, I find joy and delight;<br />\nYou make me all I can be;<br />\nI'm happiest when I'm in your light.<br /><br />I dream of you both night and day;<br />\nI'm drawn to you like the sun;<br />\nWhen you're not here, my heart feels pain;<br />\nYou are the only one.<br /><br />I think of love like this, and smile;<br />\nI never thought that I could obtain;<br />\nThe deep, excitement in my soul;<br />\nIs something I can never explain.", "id": 2}, {"time": "75000", "image": "engenn8le13ob08re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> How romantic! It's a shame that I'm not interested in him.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa:</span> Sally, who is this guy? Granted he is a bit of a wordsmith but how well do you really know him? Does he have a bit of an obsession?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> He might work in the accountant's department.  I don't see him very often and when I do, he's quite shy.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa:</span> It sounds like he has a crush on you.  You may want to talk to him.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> Should I call him or do you think it's better if I speak to him face to face.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Vanessa:</span> I think you have to consider his feelings. You should let him down gently when you see him tomorrow.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Sally:</span> I promise I won't crack up.  That would be very unkind.", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "5000", "image": "", "text": "Poetry", "id": 1}, {"time": "6000", "image": "", "text": "<span class = \"bullet\">What is poetry?</span>", "id": 2}, {"time": "35000", "image": "", "text": "<span class = \"bullet\">Different types of poetry</span>", "id": 3}, {"time": "98000", "image": "", "text": "<span class = \"bullet\">Understanding a poem</span>", "id": 4}], "video_src": "engenn8le13ob08vid01"}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "video", "id": 2, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Secret Valentine"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Say It in Rhymes"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn8le13ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " What is a poem?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " A poem is a piece of writing that is nearly always rhythmical, and often has elements such as meter, rhyme, and stanzas."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You write poetry to express your thoughts and ideas in a shorter form.<br /><br /> Sometimes, the end of each line can rhyme.<br /><br /> Here are some terms that you use when describing poetry.<br /><br />"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Word </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">  Definition </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rhyme\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" one of two or more words or phrases that end in the same sounds\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" stanza\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a group of lines in a poem\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" meter\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a way of arranging the sounds or beats in poetry \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" rhythm\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" a regular, repeated pattern of sounds or movements\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Oh, I wish that you were mine."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think about you all the time."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals for Suggestions, Necessity, and Possibility"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use modals when you want to express possibility, suggestions and necessity."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to express possibility in the past and in the future. <br />*Might suggests that something is less possible than may <br /><br /> <ul> \t<li>might / might not + infinitive</li> <li>could / could not + infinitive</li> <li>may / may not + infinitive</li> </ul> Example: <br /> <span class=\"italic\">You might be able to speak with him before work.</span><br /> <span class=\"italic\">You could be kind and friendly when you approach him.</span><br /><br /> <span class=\"strong\">Should, could, might and would are used to express suggestions:</span><br /><br /> Example: <br /> <span class=\"italic\">You should be direct with him.</span><br /> <span class=\"italic\">That would be the best way to handle the situation</span><br /><br /> The modal verbs <span class=\"strong\">must</span>, <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">have got to </span>show that something is necessary.<br /> <span class=\"strong\">Must</span> is the strongest of the three and is most common in writing. <br /><br /> <span class=\"italic\">It <span class=\"strong\">must</span> be very hard for him to speak to you.</span><br /> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> let him down softly.</span><br />"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "a long lost relative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person you have not seen or heard from in a long time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  It might be from a long lost relative."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le13ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in a conversation between friends."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to calm down"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to relax; to reduce anxiety"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Calm down and let me see. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le13ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to let someone down"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to decline someone's interest"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hope you let him down easily."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le13ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rhyme "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "one of two or more words or phrases that end in the same sounds"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The poem even rhymes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le13ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "stanza "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of lines in a poem"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are three stanzas in the poem."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le13ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wordsmith "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who is very clever at writing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Christian is a bit of a wordsmith."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le13ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "obsession "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone or something you think about constantly or frequently"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I hope I don't become an obsession of his."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le13ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to crack up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to laugh, sometimes when innapropriate"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Don't crack up when you speak with him."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn8le13ob08aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online and find 3 short poems that you like."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Complete the chart below."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Name of Poem\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Author\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Does The Poem Rhyme?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" What Is The Poem About?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" 1.\\\"}\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2.\\\"}\",\"\",\"\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"3.\\\"}\",\"\",\"\",\"\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, describe the three poems you chose aloud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use the modals <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> when talking about the poems.